00:04:42.065 --> 00:04:43.687
How to answer a coding round.

123
00:04:44.937 --> 00:04:51.913
Anchor it in the design: this sits in the redirect service's hot path, so the lookup must be O(1) and cacheable.

124
00:04:52.193 --> 00:04:57.185
State the budget: memory per item, operations per second, acceptable error.

125
00:04:57.465 --> 00:05:00.899
Probabilistic structures are chosen because of these numbers.

126
00:05:01.179 --> 00:05:03.355
Code the core and keep the I or O out.

127
00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:07.987
A map stands in for Redis or the DB, and the interviewer wants the algorithm.

128
00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:14.219
Verify with numbers: measured error versus the theoretical bound, keys moved, comparisons made.

129
00:05:14.499 --> 00:05:15.950
Each solution prints them.

130
00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:22.996
Name the production equivalent and what it adds: persistence, sharding, replication, TTLs.

